DEADWEIGHT / SHIFT 01

Game implementation, procedural score and test harness created by OpenAI
Codex for Antoni "Pingu" Norman, who supplied the toolkit and examples,
set the challenge, play-tested the game and reported performance feedback.

Built from the workflow and ideas in C Optimizer by Antoni Norman / Pingu.
https://github.com/pinguy/c_optimizer

Adapted material: ECHOHULL's bitmap font, axis-separated wall collision and
dynamic SDL loading approach. nervk informed the first-person loop and
procedural game audio; VOIDRUNNER informed the layered musical approach.

Original example material: Copyright 2026 Antoni Norman, Apache-2.0.
The new magnetic salvage mechanics, software raycaster, stereo composition,
interface and executable input/capture harness were created for this handover.
The game source is distributed under Apache-2.0; see LICENSE.

The bundled, unmodified C Optimizer build script, entry point and Python
packing tools remain MIT licensed: Copyright (c) 2026 Pinguy.
See toolkit/LICENSE. Original example game sources are not redistributed here.

No external textures, music, fonts or other runtime asset files are required.

Performance update: wall/effect caches, visibility-based floor shading,
integer colour blending, clipped sprites, accelerated SDL presentation with
software fallback, independent audio queue filling and real-time simulation.
